    <note class="self-check">
      <para>Here is a graph of \(y= f(x)\) where \(f(x) = 3x+2\).</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF 1 AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS 1 COMMA 2, 2 COMMA 4, AND 3 COMMA 8.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_17_04_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para>How do the values of \(f\) change whenever \(x\) increases by 2?</para>
    </note>
